{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/819199-poisoned-question","id":819199,"title":"Poisoned question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-29T07:03:51-08:00","id":819199,"title":"Poisoned question","content":"Just a quick question about being poisoned? Does an Uratha just take one lethal per turn by being poisoned, or one point per level of toxicity per turn ( minus primal urge)? In addition, is the effect stackable? Such as when an Uratha is bitten multiple times by a pack of poisonous rat hosts does more poison enter their system to overwhelm the victim?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T07:34:25-08:00","id":819225,"title":"","content":"I believe damage is dependent on the poison itself; werewolves can be poisoned but they also subtract their Primal Urge from the Toxicity rating. If the poison deals damage they can also spend Essence to heal it like normal and the Gauru forms healing would also apply.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure, by the RAW, if you would track each poison separately. An easier rule might be to use the highest Toxicity and add +1 to it for each additional poisonous bite received.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T07:38:04-08:00","id":819230,"title":"","content":"In combat, you don't use the full rules for poisons. Just apply the Poisoned Tilt. Out of combat, the werewolf rolls Resolve + Stamina to resist taking [Toxicity - Primal Urge] damage at intervals specified by the poison. Each success reduces the damage by 1. The type of damage is specified by the poison.<br /> <br /> Poisons don't stack. I would say if a character is suffering from multiple poisons at once, they should make rolls to resist both at their specified intervals, but being bit twice by the same poisonous Azlu is definitely not going to double the effects of the same poison. I would, however, calculate the poison's duration starting from the most recent injection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}